From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Brad Barnett <127794626+bdbarnett@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 11:40:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] extmod/modjson: A long parse lets other threads in.

json.load() and json.loads() build their whole result without letting go
of the GIL, so on a port with threads every other thread stops for as long
as the document takes to parse. On an ESP32-P4, json.loads() of a 22 KB
document on a second thread held the main thread for 50 to 63 ms, and a
thread that parsed 179 KB documents in a loop kept the main thread out for
4.9 s.

The parser now gives the GIL up after every 64 values, the way the VM does
after every few branches. Nothing else can reach the objects it has built
so far, and a thread parked there is scanned by a collection like any
other. The main thread's longest wait during the 22 KB parse is now 0 to
20 ms, and beside the 179 KB loop 40 ms. A parse with no other thread
running takes as long as before (133 ms for 29 KB on an ESP32-S3).
---
diff --git a/extmod/modjson.c b/extmod/modjson.c
index 11aedd198..2af09d8c4 100644
--- a/extmod/modjson.c
+++ b/extmod/modjson.c
@@ -156,6 +156,9 @@ static mp_obj_t mod_json_load(mp_obj_t stream_obj) {
     mp_obj_t stack_top = MP_OBJ_NULL;
     const mp_obj_type_t *stack_top_type = NULL;
     mp_obj_t stack_key = MP_OBJ_NULL;
+    #if MICROPY_PY_THREAD_GIL
+    unsigned int values = 0;
+    #endif
     S_NEXT(s);
     for (;;) {
     cont:
@@ -336,6 +339,15 @@ static mp_obj_t mod_json_load(mp_obj_t stream_obj) {
                 stack_top_type = mp_obj_get_type(stack_top);
             }
         }
+        #if MICROPY_PY_THREAD_GIL
+        // A large document takes tens of milliseconds to parse, and nothing
+        // in this loop lets go of the GIL. Let another thread in after every
+        // 64 values, as the VM does after every few branches.
+        if ((++values & 0x3f) == 0) {
+            MP_THREAD_GIL_EXIT();
+            MP_THREAD_GIL_ENTER();
+        }
+        #endif
     }
 success:
     // eat trailing whitespace
